$ORIGIN ruby-high.ai.
$TTL 300

; Cloudflare DNS import for the new Ruby High production domain.
; Import this into the ruby-high.ai zone only. It deliberately does not
; modify the existing rubyhighai.com DNS zone.
;
; These use Fly's explicit A/AAAA records instead of apex CNAME flattening
; because Fly verifies custom domains by looking for the app's IPv6 address
; unless a _fly-ownership TXT record is present.

@       IN A     66.241.124.163
@       IN AAAA  2a09:8280:1::110:305:0
www     IN A     66.241.124.163
www     IN AAAA  2a09:8280:1::110:305:0

; Fly ownership proof. Keep these if Cloudflare proxying is enabled, since
; Fly will otherwise see Cloudflare edge addresses instead of app addresses.
_fly-ownership      IN TXT   "app-56xn59q"
_fly-ownership.www  IN TXT   "app-56xn59q"

; Optional ACME DNS challenge records from `flyctl certs setup`.
; They are useful if you want Fly certificates issued before relying on
; traffic-based validation.
_acme-challenge      IN CNAME ruby-high.ai.56xn59q.flydns.net.
_acme-challenge.www  IN CNAME www.ruby-high.ai.56xn59q.flydns.net.

; Ruby High is not sending mail from this domain yet. These records make
; accidental/spoofed mail fail closed without blocking a later proper mail
; setup; replace them when a mail provider is added.
@       IN TXT   "v=spf1 -all"
_dmarc  IN TXT   "v=DMARC1; p=reject; adkim=s; aspf=s"
